  "text": "To brew coffee using a French press, follow these steps:\n1. Boil water and let it cool for one minute to reach the ideal temperature.\n2. Add one tablespoon of coarsely ground coffee per cup to the French press.\n3. Pour the hot water over the grounds, stir briefly, and place the lid on with the plunger pulled up.\n4. Wait for four minutes.\n5. Slowly press the plunger down.\n6. Serve the coffee immediately.\n\nThe bird known for its ability to repeat what you say is the parrot."
